  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a two-hour set at The Loud in Huntington, West Virginia, on Saturday, February 11, 2023 [1][3]. The event featured support from Lilly Hiatt, as noted on the promotional poster credited to Visit Huntington WV [3]. This recording, captured and transferred by Liz Hamilton, documents all twenty songs of the evening [1]. It is the only available recording of this specific performance in the Internet Archive collection [1]. The setlist spans the band’s extensive catalog, including tracks from albums such as *Get Lonely*, *Beat the Champ*, and *The Sunset Tree* [1]. \"If You See Light\" was a bustout in 248 archived shows, while \"Duke Ellington\" was a mythic rare occurrence with only two archived performances [2]. \"Green Olives\" stands out as a legendary rarity, representing the only archived performance of that song [2]. Other bustouts included \"Going to Bogota,\" \"You Were Cool,\" and \"Hair Match\" [2]. The concert concluded with a four-song encore featuring \"Heretic Pride,\" \"Green Olives,\" \"No Children,\" and \"This Year\" [1][2]. This is the 359th archived show for the band, following their previous appearance at the Doug Fir Lounge in December 2022 [2].",
